{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 69, :comments ["<b>Which YHWH commanded Moses.</b> These rebukes too were stated through direct divine speech." "<b>Besides the covenant.</b> Rashi explained: these are the curses in Mishneh Torah that were stated at Sinai, as our Sages taught in tractate Sotah: all the commandments stated in the Torah were stated, repeated, and stated a third time, and each time they were stated, they were all given with 'blessed' and 'cursed.' This is what Rashi explained: the curses in Mishneh Torah that were stated at Sinai." "<b>Which He cut with them at Horev.</b> These are the rebukes in the parashah of BeChukotai, at whose end it is written 'by the hand of Moses' — and that is Horev."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {1 "The text quotes Rashi by name, which is rendered as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:40.618261196Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}